{"archetypes":[{"name":"resume-state","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds a complex resume classifier with precedence and safety gates that are easy to misroute.","prompt_body":"Investigate the resume-state classification logic, especially precedence among blocked continuation, checkout mismatch, fresh, open PR, merged, and done paths. Check that corrupt or missing state cannot bypass branch validation, PR identity validation, or protected-branch refusal. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"github-pr","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The change depends on GitHub PR state and forked or repo-unavailable skip paths matching existing workflow semantics.","prompt_body":"Review how GitHub PR lookups, head-ref checks, forked targets, and repo-unavailable paths interact with resume routing. Look for places where stale local state can override reachable GitHub truth or where gh-skipped paths accidentally require network identity. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"ci-caps","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Session counters and cap ordering are central acceptance criteria and regressions could cause repeated or premature CI loops.","prompt_body":"Examine CI-loop counter restoration, persistence after monitor results, and iteration-cap ordering. Verify that fresh runs reset counters, open-pr resumes restore counters, and pass or already-merged outcomes are not blocked by cap checks. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"postmerge-flow","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff changes done and postmerge transitions where false terminal state could hide incomplete cleanup.","prompt_body":"Inspect merged and done resume paths plus the main CI success path for terminal-state accuracy. Check that postmerge failures preserve postmerge or stalled state and that done is written only after successful postmerge or authoritative idempotent confirmation. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"state-io","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"The new state readers and writers handle untrusted shell-style files and persisted identifiers.","prompt_body":"Review state-file parsing and writing for injection, path-scope, newline, malformed-value, and stale-marker preservation risks. Pay particular attention to PR numbers, branch names, repo values, resume markers, manifest probing, and any values later consumed by shell wrappers. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
